cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use oxo-flow in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "oxo-flow: A Rust-native bioinformatics pipeline engine"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Wang
    given-names: Shixiang
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9855-7357"
    affiliation: "Traitome"
version: 0.28.0
date-released: "2026-11-02"
license: Apache-2.0 AND LicenseRef-Proprietary
url: "https://github.com/Traitome/oxo-flow"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Traitome/oxo-flow"
keywords:
  - bioinformatics
  - pipeline
  - workflow
  - dag
  - rust
  - genomics
  - clinical
abstract: >-
  oxo-flow is a Rust-native bioinformatics pipeline engine built from first
  principles for performance, reproducibility controls, and clinical-review
  rigor. It provides DAG-based workflow execution, multi-environment
  support (conda, pixi, docker, singularity, venv), resource-aware scheduling,
  reporting designed for clinical review, and a REST API web interface.
  Clinical qualification is a separate evidence and governance process.
  The core engine, CLI, and AI crates are Apache-2.0; the web crate is
  dual-licensed (Academic/Commercial) — see LICENSE-ACADEMIC and
  LICENSE-COMMERCIAL in the repository.
